   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {The qualitative and single factor methods in land sensitivity evaluation
   always cause disadvantages such as subjectiveness, unilateralism and low
   precision. A new modified Land Sensitivity Evaluation Model (LSEM) based
   on uncertainties and grey relative relation grade is brought forward in
   this paper. Take hilly region of red soil like Changsha for example, in
   the Construction Planning for Changsha Eco-city, some ecological
   evaluation factors such as slope, groundsill carrying capacity, soil
   productivity, vegetation, soil osmosis, surface water, degree of
   resident land and scene value are selected by ecological field
   investigation with the principle of stability, independence, dominant
   and integration; the evaluation factors information are obtained with
   the help of Geography Information System(GIS) and Remote System(RS).
   Changsha urban expansion land ecological sensitivity is evaluated
   qualitatively and quantitatively by the modified land sensitivity
   evaluation model. As a result, the percentages of the permanently
   insensitive land, insensitive land, moderately sensitive land, sensitive
   land and highly sensitive land are respectively 14.77\%, 16.64\%,
   24.07\%, 30.91\% and 13.61\%; most land of Changsha is suitable for
   construction (the total percentage of permanently insensitive,
   insensitive and moderately sensitive land is 55.48\%), but ecological
   environment must be protected in construction.},
