   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {This paper presents some initial results of geotechnical investigations
   of urban solid waste both in situ and in the laboratory. The waste
   studied came from Bandeirantes waste fill (Sao Paulo - Brazil) and is
   about 15 years old. A synthesis of cone penetration tests is showed and
   the results of consolidate-drained triaxial compression tests and
   confined compression tests on large samples are also presented. Shear
   strength parameters seem to be dependent on deformation and the waste
   showed large secondary compression. Some remarks on conception, design
   and construction of an experimental test fill, as well as, some
   preliminary results of compaction on a test fill are also shown.},
