Note = {2nd World Conference on Psychology, Counselling and Guidance (WCPCG),
   Antalya, TURKEY, MAY 25-29, 2011},
Abstract = {Reviews of research on religion and health have concluded that at least
   some types of religious behaviours are related to higher levels of
   physical and mental health. The objective of this paper is to display
   and demonstrate how religion can be directly effective on human health.
   Giving a religious understanding of human being and his nature, the
   writers point out that there are two general sorts of needs and
   requirements : bodily and non-bodily. Once any kind of these
   requirements are neglected, some sort of disorder and crisis are
   emerged. An explanation is given to defend that when non-bodily needs
   are overlooked the emergence of psychological disorder is expectable.
   According to Islamic perspective there are many ways that we could keep
   our life saved from illness and psychological disorder. Praying as a
   first value advice in Quranic verses plays an effective role to provide
   human being with health and calm life. On the basis of Islamic teachings
   a detail explanation regarding relationship between faith and
   psychological health is given. The connection between faith and
   psychological health in this paper is based on particular kind of human
   nature. (C) 2011 Published by Elsevier Ltd. Selection and/or peer-review
   under responsibility of the 2nd World Conference on Psychology,
