Organization = {Portuguese Soc Occupat Safety \& Hygiene; Univ Minho, Sch Engn; Univ
   Porto, Fac Engn; Univ Lisbon, Fac Human Kinet; Polytechn Univ Catalonia;
   Tech Univ Delft; Faculdade Motricidade Humana; DELTA; EXIM; ACT;
   European Agcy Safety \& Hlth Work; Lavoro},
Abstract = {Motorcycle police officers are exposed to different environmental
   conditions, resulting in a range of situations that may be harmful to
   their health and job performance. The perception of the effects of noise
   at work can help minimizing risks; and identify portions of a greater
   likehood of developing diseases. The purpose of this article is to
   present the results of an investigation about noise perception of
   Motorcycle police officers in their daily activities. The study sample
   was 46 male police officers from Joao Pessoa-Brazil with more than 3
   years of service. Data was collected through measurement of noise levels
   and application of a perception questionnaire. The measurements of noise
   point to levels above the Brazilian standards. The questionnaire
   results, suggest that the perception of police about the noise is clear,
   and they considered noise exposure as a bad condition that interferes on
   their performance, activities and on health status.},
