Note = {Advancement on Informatics, Business and Management International
   Conference (AIBMIC), Bandung, INDONESIA, MAY 31-JUN 02, 2016},
Organization = {Malaysia Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {This study aims to determine the perception of Bachelor of Arts in
   Communication (AB in Communication) interns on their internship program
   in terms of the importance of internship, the influence of their
   supervisors and the learning benefits they gained based on their
   experience. Survey and interview were conducted to the respondents.
   Respondents are student interns of Calamba City, Laguna taking AB in
   Communication. The student interns agreed that internship program is
   significant and it provides students many learning benefits. Student
   interns agreed that internship helps them decide the right job they
   would take in the future, provides them real work experience, enhances
   their skills and gives them new knowledge, hones their personality and
   work ethics and enhances curriculum. Also, the interns consider their
   supervisors as their mentors during their training. Based on the results
   of the study, there is significant difference in the perception of AB
   Communication interns when they are grouped according to age.},
