Year = {2016},
Pages = {669-677},
Note = {5th International Conference on Cognitive Neurodynamics (ICCN), Sanya,
   PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 03-07, 2015},
Organization = {East China Univ Sci \& Technol, Inst Cognit Neurodynam; Chinese Soc
   Theoret \& Appl Mech; Brain Engn Soc Korea; Tamagawa Univ, Brain Sci
   Ctr; KAIST, Brain Sci Res Ctr; Int Neural Network Soc; Japan Soc Neural
   Network; Shanghai Soc Nonlinear Sci; Natl Nat Sci Fdn China},
Abstract = {The research on neural code theory of gait movement under visual
   perception has important significance for understanding brain working
   mechanisms of sensory input, cognitive process or motor output, and for
   future applications of artificial intelligence or brain-computer
   interface. In this review, we first summarize several common types of
   codes used in studying visual perception. Through comparing advantages
   and disadvantages of these codes, we try to find an efficient code which
   could interpret perceptional behavior in different levels. Then, we
   analyze the theory of gait movement output under visual perception
   condition, that is gait movement output affected by cerebral cortex
   signal, to provide certain scientific evidence for practical application
   of intelligent robot with real neural control principle of human body
   motion and thereby build biological neural network models that conform
   with human gait movement mechanism. Finally, we introduce a new cortical
   coding mode with widely used prospect-neural energy code.},
