Organization = {European Soc Computat Methods Sci \& Engn},
Abstract = {The study aims to show the results of research on the formation of the
   sacred landscape of Bydgoszcz. Regarding population, it is the eighth
   city of Poland and the largest in Kujawsko-Pomorskie Voivodeship. The
   research problem was considered in the contemporary city limits. Sacred
   buildings were catalogued and grouped according to four periods of time.
   Fieldwork allowed to collect data about objects and their location,
   which was the input data for further work in the GIS environment.
   Location maps of individual facilities and time availability models for
   pedestrians and motorists were developed. Due to their architectural
   diversity, sacred buildings are valuable elements of cultural heritage
   with outstanding aesthetic qualities. In most cases, these objects
   harmoniously blend into the contemporary image of the city, providing it
   with a classic character. The cultural landscape is in the form of an
   absolute sacrum, which is the dominance of material objects such as
   churches and cemeteries.},
