   Cochlear Implant Team},
Abstract = {Valid tests of auditory capacity in young children with hearing loss are
   needed to distinguish capacity from performance, to guide sensory and
   habilitative intervention, to contribute to outcome assessment and to
   promote evidence-based practice. Behavioral tests of auditory capacity
   are confounded by non-auditory factors, leading to age and experience
   effects that are difficult to interpret. Electrophysiological responses
   to acoustic change during an ongoing stimulus (the Acoustic Change
   Complex {[}ACC]) may provide an objective alternative. (c) 2004 Elsevier
