Note = {20th Regular Meeting of the Barany-Society, WURZBURG, GERMANY, SEP
   12-15, 1998},
Organization = {Barany Soc},
Abstract = {In daily pedaudiologic Practice children who are brought to examination
   often complain of ``vertigo{''}. They have problems with body
   coordination in their medical history They are unstable on their legs,
   often stumbles, have problems during bicycling or skating, get bad marks
   for sport activities in school, have problems with concentration, are
   easy to divert and sometimes they give the impression that they have a
   hearing disorder.
   Disturbances of central sensory perception should not be seen isolated
   because they are often an expression of problems in several sensory
   subsystems. One can also talk in this context of problems or
   disturbances of sensory integration of various sensory stimuli.
   This paper deals with neurootologic test results of 25 children with
   problems in the field of central sensory perception, The neurootological
   routine tests did not show pathological findings. More sensitive tests
   were, however vestibulospinal examinations as Romberg,
   Unterberger/Fukuda stepping test, and dynamic posturography.},
