   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {OH reactivity which is defined as a sum of reaction rates of each
   reactive chemical species with OH radicals provides quite useful
   information about air quality as index of photochemical activity in the
   atmosphere. Directly observed OH reactivity and sum up of the OH
   reactivity of each trace species were observed in suburban of Tokyo on
   May 25, 26, 29, in 2009. There were considerable difference between
   directly observed and sum upped OH reactivity. The concentrations of
   each VOCs in the urban air are required to know the OH reactivity in the
   atmosphere. Concentrations of VOCs were measured by GC-FID analysis.
   There are considerable numbers of unidentified peaks of volatile organic
   compounds (VOCs) generally detected when urban air samples were analysed
   by a GC-FID technique. The contribution of unidentified VOCs was
   estimated by comparative reaction method using GC-FID. The contribution
   of the unidentified VOCs was about 6\% of the total OH reactivity. This
   improves the difference of directly measured and sum upped OH reactivity
   in some extend, but most of difference was still unknown. Other species
   which can not detected by GC-FID would be contribute this difference.},
