   ENGLAND, MAY   06, 1992},
Organization = {ERGON SOC; DESIGN AGE},
Abstract = {Especially in stressful urban environments, a `transgenerational'
   approach to design for older people can yield general benefits to
   society. Portable maps to aid orientation, type that is more easily
   scanned, and a more inviting, as well as aurally sensitive, attitude to
   IT would also represent useful steps forward. In both the modification
   of old products and in design for compressed morbidity, there is a need
   for methods which encourage activity instead of just moderating the
   effects of infirmity. Last but not least, old people themselves need to
   become a design resource.},
