   Environmental Management - Tourism, Society and Education Session,
   Tokyo, JAPAN, JUN 29-30, 2013},
Organization = {TU Bergakademie Freiberg; Tianjin Univ Finance Econ, Tourism Dept;
   Waseda Univ; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {Under the background of global climate changing, every urban region is
   seeking more ideal development mode. How to guide China's urban tourism
   resources development and protection with low carbon economy principles
   is a very real and urgent question. This article starts from the
   searching for the relationship between low carbon economy and urban
   development, then analyses that the implementation of low carbon economy
   is the inevitable choice for development \& protection of urban tourism
   resources. Only by reasonable planning and layout on urban tourism
   resources, making full use of climatic conditions, considering the
   ecological load capacity in urban regions, controlling the tourism
   resources damage systematically, using cultural element to reflect the
   special features and themes of a city, reducing carbon emission levels
   through applying the low carbon technologies into tourist traffic and
   other major aspects, and guiding urban residents and tourists to low
   carbon consumption, can the sustainable development of urban tourism
   resources be achieved ultimately.},
