   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {The present work examines various aspects of hydrogeological hazards
   present in the city of Morelia (state of Michoacan, Mexico) with a
   particular eye on the Paloma scarp, located in the southern part of the
   urban area and on the flood plain of the Rio Chiquito. The Paloma scarp
   has been studied from a geologic, geomorphological and geomechanical
   point of view in order to assess landslide hazard while of the Rio
   Chiquito flood plain, hydrologic and hydraulic aspects have been
   analyzed, enabling a flood hazard assessment. The rapid expansion of the
   city in the last decades has lead to the urbanization of areas highly
   susceptible to hydrological processes determining high risk conditions
   for human lives and property. For the hydraulic modeling of the Rio
   Chiquito HEC-RAS software was utilized assuming stationary flow
   conditions.},
