Note = {4th International Conference on Management, Hotel and Tourism and
   Accounting (IMHA), Paris Van Java, Indonesia, Bandung, INDONESIA, 2014},
Organization = {Bina Nusantara Univ, Sch Business Management; PT Telekomunikasi
   Indonesia; Intel Educ; Asus; Acer},
Abstract = {The development of e-money services creates a lot of terminology to
   emerge. Different companies use different terms to explain the new
   services in their brand communication. Consequently, the development of
   emoney market is not followed by increasing consumer understanding.
   There are indications on misconceptions of consumers against this modern
   way of payment. This study investigated more closely how companies
   constantly talk to their target audience in their marketing
   communication and contrast it with how consumers understand the concept
   of various emoney format and the benefits for their daily life. The
   results of this study provide insights for actors in e-money business on
   how to start educate consumers in a better way, to reduce the remaining
   barriers in consumer mind that hinder the adoption of this e-money
   services. Research conducted through series of qualitative study:
   netnography exploration, content analysis of various company brand
   communication and in-depth interview with target audience of e-money.},
